    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d808">

                <pb facs="0963" n="883" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg883"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Merry to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">San
                                José</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1902-03-01"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">March 1, 1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 694.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to advise the return to
                    San Salvador on February 16 of President Begalado after a brief visit to
                    Guatemala City. * * * I am also informed from Managua that the President of
                    Guatemala has joined in the arbitration treaty signed at the Corinto conference
                    on January 20, 1902, by the Presidents of Nicaragua, Costa Rica, Salvador, and
                    Honduras, in accordance with his promise to President Iglesias. * * * The peace
                    of Central America now appears assured in the near future. * * *</p>
                <p>With assurances, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William Lawrence
                    Merry.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
